1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,315
Hello, Sandy.

2
00:00:01,315 --> 00:00:03,560
How have you been getting on with your dissertation?

3
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:03,610
Fine,

4
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:08,034
and I've been working hard on the various action points we agreed on our

5
00:00:08,034 --> 00:00:08,630
last tutorial.

6
00:00:08,630 --> 00:00:10,800
Do you want to talk me through what you've done?

7
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:11,519
Yeah, sure.

8
00:00:11,519 --> 00:00:15,835
Well, we agreed on three main targets for me to aim for.

9
00:00:15,835 --> 00:00:20,150
The first one was to find out about suitable data analysis software.

10
00:00:20,150 --> 00:00:20,770
Yes.

11
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:25,060
And what I decided to do was to look through catalogues specializing in IT.

12
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:26,108
That's a good idea.

13
00:00:26,108 --> 00:00:27,680
What did you come up with?

14
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:30,310
I found the names of two promising ones.

15
00:00:30,310 --> 00:00:30,770
Right.

16
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:34,200
But I also thought it'd be worthwhile talking to a lecturer.

17
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,047
Oh right.

18
00:00:35,047 --> 00:00:36,740
Who did you see?

19
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:37,533
Jane Prince.

20
00:00:37,533 --> 00:00:39,118
Do you know her?

21
00:00:39,118 --> 00:00:41,100
She's in the Computer Centre.

22
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,490
Yes, of course, she's the new Head.

23
00:00:43,490 --> 00:00:43,808
Yes.

24
00:00:43,808 --> 00:00:45,400
Well, she was very helpful.

25
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:45,778
Oh,

26
00:00:45,778 --> 00:00:46,533
that's good.

27
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:48,800
Did she suggest anything in particular?

28
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:49,122
Yeah.

29
00:00:49,122 --> 00:00:53,622
She recommended software called Vivat and said I should book up for a couple

30
00:00:53,622 --> 00:00:55,230
of practice sessions using Vivat.

31
00:00:55,230 --> 00:00:55,531
Great.

32
00:00:55,531 --> 00:00:57,340
I'm sure you'll find them useful.

33
00:00:57,340 --> 00:01:02,231
And, of course, the second target was to draw up a survey checklist which

34
00:01:02,231 --> 00:01:02,580
I...

35
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:05,140
Yes, you emailed me it last week.

36
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,630
Have you had a chance to look...?

37
00:01:06,630 --> 00:01:09,510
Of course, um I think it's good.

38
00:01:09,510 --> 00:01:11,978
Very much on the right lines.

39
00:01:11,978 --> 00:01:15,680
I'd say your first two sections are spot on.

40
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:18,971
I wouldn't suggest that you change anything there,

41
00:01:18,971 --> 00:01:24,730
but in section three you really do need to have questions on teaching experience.

42
00:01:24,730 --> 00:01:25,002
Yeah.

43
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:27,450
I was thinking that section looked a bit short.

44
00:01:27,450 --> 00:01:28,000
Right.

45
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,030
And my third target was, do further reading on discipline.

46
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:33,544
Oh yes.

47
00:01:33,544 --> 00:01:35,600
I mentioned a couple of writers, didn't I?

48
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:39,545
Yes, well I got hold of the Banerjee and I thought that was excellent.

49
00:01:39,545 --> 00:01:43,490
But I'm afraid I didn't manage to get hold of the essays about classroom

50
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:45,463
management-you know, the ones by Simon Ericsson.

51
00:01:45,463 --> 00:01:49,408
The bookshop said it was out of print and the library doesn't have a

52
00:01:49,408 --> 00:01:49,690
copy.

53
00:01:49,690 --> 00:01:50,390
Oh right,

54
00:01:50,390 --> 00:01:53,893
and I'm afraid I've lent my copy to another student.

55
00:01:53,893 --> 00:01:58,796
What I suggest you do is try the library again-this time apply for it

56
00:01:58,796 --> 00:02:00,897
through the service called special loans.

57
00:02:00,897 --> 00:02:02,648
Have you done that before?

58
00:02:02,648 --> 00:02:05,100
You're entitled to six books a year.

59
00:02:05,100 --> 00:02:05,514
Yes.

60
00:02:05,514 --> 00:02:06,343
No problem.

61
00:02:06,343 --> 00:02:08,000
That's what I'll do.

62
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,250
So, lots of useful work done.

63
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:13,140
So, let's look at some new targets.

64
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:17,268
We'll start by having a chat about your Chapter One.

65
00:02:17,268 --> 00:02:19,745
I very much enjoyed reading it.

66
00:02:19,745 --> 00:02:25,525
Your written style is very clear and you've included lots of interesting descriptions of

67
00:02:25,525 --> 00:02:27,589
education in your target area.

68
00:02:27,589 --> 00:02:32,130
I've just got a couple of suggestions for some additional work.

69
00:02:32,130 --> 00:02:32,759
Of course.

70
00:02:32,759 --> 00:02:36,530
Could I just ask - what do you think I should call it?

71
00:02:36,530 --> 00:02:39,443
Well, I'd go for something like Context Review.

72
00:02:39,443 --> 00:02:40,900
What do you think?

73
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:42,880
Well, short and to the point.

74
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:43,228
Exactly.

75
00:02:43,228 --> 00:02:48,095
Now, as regards specific areas to work on, I'd be quite interested to have

76
00:02:48,095 --> 00:02:51,920
a few more statistics about the schools in the different zones.

77
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:52,135
Oh,

78
00:02:52,135 --> 00:02:53,212
that wouldn't be a problem.

79
00:02:53,212 --> 00:02:54,720
I can get them from the Internet.

80
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:55,044
Great,

81
00:02:55,044 --> 00:02:59,581
and although you did make a reference to quite a few different writers, I

82
00:02:59,581 --> 00:03:03,470
think you should aim to cite more works written later than 2000.

83
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:03,843
OK.

84
00:03:03,843 --> 00:03:04,961
That's more difficult,

85
00:03:04,961 --> 00:03:06,451
but I can try.

86
00:03:06,451 --> 00:03:09,060
When do you want that done by?

87
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:10,325
Oh, it's not urgent.

88
00:03:10,325 --> 00:03:13,172
Um I should aim for the end of term.

89
00:03:13,172 --> 00:03:17,600
But in the meantime, I think you should also be thinking about Chapter Two.

90
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,630
Should I be drafting it already?

91
00:03:19,630 --> 00:03:19,894
No,

92
00:03:19,894 --> 00:03:22,530
but I think you should note down its main sections.

93
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:22,891
Yes.

94
00:03:22,891 --> 00:03:26,140
You know, I always find that the hardest part.

95
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:29,600
I always find it helpful to put some ideas on index cards.

96
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:30,200
Yeah.

97
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:30,474
Um...

98
00:03:30,474 --> 00:03:32,116
and then you can sort them,

99
00:03:32,116 --> 00:03:34,305
and even lay them out on the floor.

100
00:03:34,305 --> 00:03:35,400
It's a real help.

101
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,162
Well, I'll certainly try it!

102
00:03:37,162 --> 00:03:39,630
When would the deadline be for that?

103
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:44,355
My advice would be to get it done before you embark upon the research.

104
00:03:44,355 --> 00:03:47,730
You can always change it later if you need to.

105
00:03:47,730 --> 00:03:47,964
OK.

106
00:03:47,964 --> 00:03:49,370
I'll get going on that then.
